.Dd October 18, 2026
.Dt DO-SCREENSHOT 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm do-screenshot
.Nd screenshot the X11 desktop, an area or the active window
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl d Ar dir
.Op Cm desktop | area | window | Cm delay Op Ar seconds
.Nm
.Fl h
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
takes a screenshot under X11 with
.Xr maim 1 ,
saves it as a PNG, copies it to the clipboard and announces it in a
notification.
The mode says what is captured:
.Bl -tag -width "delay [seconds]"
.It Cm desktop
The whole X screen, every output.
.It Cm area
A rectangle, or a window, picked with the mouse.
.It Cm window
The window that has the focus.
.It Cm delay Op Ar seconds
The window that has the focus
.Ar seconds
from now, 5 by default: time to switch to it.
The wait is counted down in a notification, replaced each second.
.El
.Pp
Without a mode, one is picked from a
.Xr rofi 1
menu, so a key binding or a bar button can run
.Nm
bare.
A menu dismissed is not an error, and takes no screenshot.
.Pp
The file is
.Pa Screenshot_YYYY-MM-DD-HH-MM-SS.png
in the directory of
.Fl d ,
else
.Ev XDG_PICTURES_DIR ,
else
.Pa ~/Pictures ,
which is created if need be.
A name already taken gets a
.Ql -2 ,
.Ql -3
\&... suffix; the name is claimed by creating the file, so two shots in
the same second cannot pick the same one.
Its path is printed on stdout.
A capture that fails, such as an area selection cancelled, removes the
file, so a failure never leaves an empty PNG behind.
.Pp
Only
.Xr maim 1
is required, and
.Xr xdotool 1
to find the active window.
The clipboard and the notification are what follow a screenshot, not
the screenshot itself: without
.Xr xclip 1
or
.Xr notify-send 1 ,
.Nm
says on stderr what it skipped, and still succeeds.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width "-d dir"
.It Fl d Ar dir
Save into
.Ar dir .
.It Fl h
Print the usage and exit.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width XDG_PICTURES_DIR
.It Ev XDG_PICTURES_DIR
The directory screenshots are saved into, unless
.Fl d .
.It Ev HOME
Where
.Pa ~/Pictures
is, without either.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It 0
The screenshot was saved, or the menu was dismissed.
.It 1
No screenshot was taken: an area selection cancelled, an answer typed
into the menu that is no mode, no
.Xr rofi 1
to ask for a mode,
.Xr maim 1
or
.Xr xdotool 1
missing or failing, or a directory that cannot be created.
.It 2
A usage error.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
In
.Xr i3 1 ,
the menu on the Print key:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
bindsym --release Print exec --no-startup-id do-screenshot
.Ed
.Pp
The focused window in ten seconds, into a directory of its own:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ do-screenshot -d ~/shots delay 10
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr maim 1 ,
.Xr notify-send 1 ,
.Xr rofi 1 ,
.Xr xclip 1 ,
.Xr xdotool 1
.Sh CAVEATS
.Nm
works under X11 only.
Its menu is
.Xr rofi 1 Ns 's
plain dmenu, styled only by
.Xr rofi 1 Ns 's
own configuration.
